WEBVTT

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.500
Mew-Mew!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.830
Miyako.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.580
Has it come out yet?

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.290
Nope. We're still waiting.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.200
Is it me, or is that sound louder
each day we're here?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.790
It's so scary!

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.580
Maybe I've gotten used to it.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.790
It is taking its sweet time to come out.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.160
A difficult birth, perhaps.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.330
What if it's delaying
because the Order is awful?

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.870
It isn't a human.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.200
"PARTICIPATE IN THE ITF"

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.200
"ITF"?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.790
Idol Tokyo Festival?

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.870
We'll make the arrangements for the ITF
as per the Order.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.620
"Just Flip It Over!"

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:56.040
Is it just me, or is Goudacchi
a little robotic these days?

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.830
He's almost brutally docile.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:00.950
Whatever he says is absolutely hilarious!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.080
A gorilla robot?

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.790
ITF is that idol event
that happens every year, right?

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.160
This year's event begins next week
and will go on for two days.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.910
It's been called the idol launchpad,
since many groups get noticed there.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:17.540
If you want a bunch of new fans,
you perform at the ITF.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.540
You know all this stuff, don't you, Nicole?

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.040
It's common knowledge.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.120
One week from now.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.290
No matter how powerful the Wall is,
with one week's notice, there's no way.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.080
Whoa! So this is the ITF?

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.620
There's a crazy amount of people here!

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.040
And a lot of idols here, too.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.700
I can't believe we actually got in.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.500
If this were a manga,
the Internet would be flaming us now.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.040
You get the feeling there's a bigger force
working behind the scenes.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.830
Mr. Wall sure is amazing!

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.330
Y-Yeah.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.790
Wow, all these other idols' outfits are so cute!

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.660
Memories, let's go!

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.620
Circles are amazing!

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.250
So much team spirit!

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.410
Hey, we should do the same thing!

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.790
It looks like it's about to start.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.540
Come on, get ready!

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.330
We're going in.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.910
Man, Nono, the way you sleep is just the worst!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.870
Hey, stop that.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.330
There sure are a lot of you guys out there.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.910
So tell us, Reika.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.620
Do you have any stories about 22/7
that you'd like to tell us?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:43.120
Um...

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:48.540
W-We just get on so well.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.870
To the point where we
always want to be together.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.660
Really? Could you tell us any interesting
behind-the-scenes stories about your members?

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:04.950
Seriously? Y'all don't have
any stories about us?

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.700
I don't believe that for one second.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.290
We're very close, but don't get
the wrong idea, folks.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:19.120
Who knew the majestic Reika
would get flustered and space out?

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:25.200
It was my first time in front of so many people.
Of course I'd get nervous.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.580
Toda, could you stop overdoing it
with things just a bit?

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.580
Anyway, it wasn't like you could produce
a juicy story for the MC, either!

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.330
It's not like we could work
with what you were giving us.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:33.120
Why would I? The crowd had a good laugh.
Everyone's happy.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.120
Man, we really don't
get along, do we?

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.290
You kind of became a hindrance
to the process.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.290
It wasn't like you were helping, either!

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.330
It isn't cute when you
pretend to get tough.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.750
W-Wait a second, guys.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:42.950
I'm not! You're the one
who's trying to pick a fight with me!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.950
It is confusing how they put us together
and expected us to get along.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.580
And now we're backtracking, huh?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.580
Sure. Fine. Whatever.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.200
Stop!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.540
"ONE YEAR AGO"

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.120
But, Big Sis!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.790
It's Isamu's fault, since he broke my toy!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.410
It's your fault, Takeru! You hogged it first!

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:06.830
Kaoru keeps taking my doll away from me!

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.200
There, now play.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.620
But this really isn't Mero now!

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.160
No, this is too scary!

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.410
Combine!

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.580
They're back to playing?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.660
I'm Kono Miyako, and I'm the eldest
of seven brothers and sisters.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:38.950
But we're not related by blood.
You could say that they're my half-siblings.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:39.830
Oh, dear...

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:43.830
My mom's a real odd duck.
She's been divorced four times.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:47.370
She's so carefree.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.450
Wow!

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.790
Mess it up again, and you're getting beat.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:52.830
I'm home!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.120
Oh, Mom!

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.410
Hey, Miyako.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:58.580
Welcome home, Mom!
I missed you!

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.000
Aren't you supposed to be
in your rebellious phase?

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.040
Aren't you too calm for just getting off work?

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.500
Who're you callin' four times divorced? Not me!

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.120
I haven't cried a single tear over you.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.410
Perfect!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.200
Wow, they're having a lying contest!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.250
Okay, enough of that. Bath time!

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.450
We'll be packed in like sardines!
I can barely fit up to my shoulders!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:20.450
Ah, now that's my rebellious teenager
I know and love.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.450
What? An <i>okonomiyaki</i> party?

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:24.370
That's right!

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.950
22/7 needs more solidarity.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:30.750
Otherwise, we're gonna get wrecked
at the idol festival tomorrow.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.200
But it's not like
we dislike each other or anything.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.500
True, but that's not the problem here.
We're not as close as we need to be.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.290
We couldn't answer any questions
during the interview.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:42.120
For an idol group, that can be fatal.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.120
So, we need to have
a friendly little get-together.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.080
I don't really like <i>okonomiyaki</i> , though.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.950
That's not the point!

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:53.750
Quite frankly, I don't have
much faith in you, Kono.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.540
That's a lie, you know you love me.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.450
Put Baby Star Ramen in it!

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.330
That's the spirit!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.410
You should join us, Nicole!

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:04.250
Huh?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.750
Yes! It's decided, then.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.580
I'm looking forward
to this get-together a bit now!

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.750
I gotta think about what I want in mine!

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:08.750
Oh, y-yeah.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.330
So where should we do this?

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.540
My sweet home.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.000
This place looks dignified.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.950
Ah, that's right, this is your first time
going to a dorm, isn't it, Miu?

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:25.410
It's the same for me and Saito.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.620
Is that so?

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.950
Welcome to the garden of maidens!

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.910
Wheat flour, cabbage, pork, eggs,

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.120
green onions, tenkasu tempura bits,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.120
red pickled ginger...

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.250
...and one of the three sacred treasures
of the Kono household!

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.830
You're like a hero!

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.500
Aren't those just regular tools?

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.250
No, I brought these from home.

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.500
The hot plate, too?

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.370
Yep!

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.200
What if they make <i>okonomiyaki</i> at home?

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.250
Then I bring it home to them.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.120
That's irrational.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.000
Just can't make good <i>okonomiyaki</i>
without this.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.620
Miyako's getting hyped, huh?

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.830
Right?

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:17.950
Y'all can't mix it all messy that way!
You gotta mix it smoothly.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.290
Think of it like a baby.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.620
Would you move a baby around
all crazy like that?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.160
But you can't mix a baby!

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.040
Boop!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.700
How can I help you, Toda?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.200
I just booped you.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.080
That makes no sense.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.410
Boop!

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.950
Is that right? Then mix this for me.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.080
Roger!

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.000
It's a boop!

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.750
Sure wasn't the reaction I was expecting.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.910
Hey, Mew-Mew, come help out some!

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.620
Okay!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.120
Alright! Time to grill, everyone!

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.540
It looks so good!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.080
It's too early to flip it.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.660
Yeah, it's probably still cooking.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.200
Are we having <i>okonomiyaki</i> again?

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.540
What are you saying?

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:19.410
It's cheap! It's fast!
It's delicious! It fills you up!

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.160
Four birds, one stone!

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.160
You just can't cook anything else, can you?

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.080
Miyako's just bad at it.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.410
That hurts...

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.540
Where's Mom?

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.040
Asleep. She just got home.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:36.790
Something about some trouble at work.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.450
Mom? I brought you some <i>okonomiyaki</i> .

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.950
She's dug out her old mobile phone again.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.750
She's crying.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.160
Maybe I'll draw a mustache on her.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.040
Dad...

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:02.500
Oh, Mom, not again.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:08.950
I told y'all! If ya can't pay,
I'll pull it out of your butt!

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.950
I love them so much, the little brats.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:18.080
Goodness. What is she
yelling about in her sleep?

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:24.410
Oh, no.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.000
This will break us.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.290
Oh, no.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.950
I get it now.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:33.700
You want to live on your own
as a fashion designer?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:37.500
Yeah. I really love making clothes.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:43.790
And that's why I'd like to go to Tokyo,
so I can study it in a proper school setting.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:46.660
Tokyo, huh?

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.950
I haven't told my family yet.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.200
"MIYAKO KONO"

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.040
Entertainment? That sounds nice.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.040
Get Mr. Oguri's autograph for me.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:08.540
What are you thinking, Mom?

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.950
There's no way I could become an idol!

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:13.620
And it sure as heck ain't gonna be that easy!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.120
Plus, moving me to Tokyo
is gonna cost money.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:20.450
I'd like to see them send a letter after they've
seen our standard of living in this house.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.330
Are you sure about that?

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:29.120
Which reminds me, you had
your career consultation today, didn't you?

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:31.950
"SILENCE IS GOLDEN"

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.950
Did you tell them
you wanted to be a pro boxer?

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.250
I told them I wanted to be a space cop.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.660
I'm gonna protect both the peace
of the universe and our family!

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.410
I can't seem to throw it away.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:05.410
And Mom wants to see Dad.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:08.700
That's a good boy! You're so cute!

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:13.250
You're cute too, Miyako!

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:18.120
If I were to leave home,
only Dad could replace me.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.370
I'm looking for this guy.

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:25.830
I have no clue. Did something happen?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.250
No.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:28.580
That's not exactly it.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:31.290
I've looked high and low
and can't seem to find him.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.040
He's changed his address a lot, too.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.120
"MOTHER AND CHILD
 REUNITE AFTER 30 YEARS"

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.410
I missed you!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:36.120
I missed you, too!

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.660
Not even a day went by--

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.000
I'm so glad!

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:45.080
If I ever become famous...

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.120
...I wonder if that's when
I'll be able to find Dad.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.160
What the heck am I doing thinking like this?

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.540
Bedtime.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.370
"SHOPPING TOWN"

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.450
I'm home!

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:40.500
Welcome home. You're back awfully late.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.370
Didn't I tell you?
The space cop was on patrol!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:49.620
Maybe I should start investing.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:54.830
Why don't you?
If we have the money to, that is.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.790
Here.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.910
"100,000 YEN
(THAT MOM SWEATED
AND WORKED HARD TO GET)"

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.410
Are you gonna be buying out an I.T. company?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.450
There's something patronizing
on that envelope.

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:07.620
I'm investing in an idol named Miyako Kono.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:10.080
What? Why in me?

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:15.700
Because I know you've stared at that envelope
every night before you go to bed.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:20.330
I had no idea you wanted
to become an idol so badly.

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:24.200
It's time to start living for yourself
and follow your own dreams.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.410
She's way off the mark on that one, but...

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:32.410
I guess we really are alike.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:36.950
The other brats have gotten older,
and we'll find a way to manage.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:40.290
You're the one worried about them, not me.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:46.620
I won't let any harm come to y'all.
I wanna go be an idol for a bit.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.750
Just for a little bit.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.200
What I'm going to become is a space pirate.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.540
Weren't you gonna become a space detective?

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:56.290
They're similar, okay!

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:01.790
Miyako is on her way to Tokyo!

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:05.370
I'll just be working away from home,
and I'll be back.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.040
What? No!

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:10.410
Takeru's so bad at flipping the <i>okonomiyaki</i>
when we make it!

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:11.500
What'd you say?!

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:14.000
Sheesh, you two just can't stop fighting.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.120
Listen up.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:18.370
I'm about to lay some knowledge on you
with a proverb.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.370
Yay, a proverb!

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.000
What's a proverb?

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.450
It's true we're only half-siblings.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:28.580
Half?

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:31.080
It means our Dads are different.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:35.040
That's correct. It means we all share
the same Mom, but not the same Dad.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:36.620
But take a look at this.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.290
This cabbage was grown in Aichi Prefecture.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.790
And this pork was raised in Chiba Prefecture...

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.080
That was so good!

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:51.620
It wasn't bad. I think that's
the first time I've eaten without an occasion.

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:53.040
Wow, that's so weird!

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.250
I don't want to hear that
from you of all people.

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.660
Yummy, tummy, delicious!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.120
I was making cheese fondue.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.750
It's been a while since I last had
some good <i>okonomiyaki</i> .

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:00.750
Let's make some
cheese fondue <i>okonomiyaki</i> next!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:04.250
It's been a minute since I had <i>okonomiyaki</i> ,
especially without an occasion.

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:04.250
Dad always did say they gave you a real bang
for your buck when he made it for us.

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:08.040
It's more delicious when you have lots
of people to sit with when you have it.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.040
Mom used to make it
a lot for us before.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:12.080
Really? I guess that's universal
throughout Japan, then.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:12.080
Right? I feel that way, too, for real.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.120
It's nice to be loud and happy with everyone!

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.120
Did you have fun, Mew-Mew?

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:18.450
--I feel the same way.
--Me, too.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:18.450
Yeah, I did. You're so good
at making <i>okonomiyaki</i> , Miyako.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:21.250
Right?

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:24.410
Listen up.
I'll lay some knowledge on you with a proverb.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.040
This cabbage was grown in Gunma.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:31.950
And this pork was raised in Kagoshima.

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:34.000
This wheat flour is from Hokkaido.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.000
This Chinese yam is from Saitama.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.580
The <i>tenkasu</i> tempura is from Tokyo.
This pickled ginger is from Thailand.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.370
This dried shrimp is from Shizuoka.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.160
These eggs are laid in Ibaraki.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.700
Like us, these were all born and raised
in different places.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:48.870
Our personalities and
characteristics are different.

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:52.500
At first, we weren't sure if we
would mesh together, and we fought a lot.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:57.870
But you see? Mix us up, slap us on a grill,
flip us over, and we come out just fine!

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:02.120
My next question is for Reika.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.410
Okay!

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:04.660
Let's see...

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:08.700
Have you and the other members
done anything interesting together recently?

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.250
Yes.

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:13.700
The other day we had an <i>okonomiyaki</i> party.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.450
It was so much fun!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.700
That was when we found out
that Reika has a thing for dads.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.290
D-Dads?

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:21.500
You prefer dads?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.040
N-Not at all!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:26.040
But don't you have a dad waiting for you?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.370
Yikes.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.660
Isn't it normal for your Dad to wait for you?

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:33.410
You sure that's the case there, buddy?

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.290
I told you, yes, it's fine!

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.700
What about you, Takigawa?

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:39.040
How was your <i>okonomiyaki</i> party?

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.910
Uh, um...

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:52.910
...yesterday, Miyako booped me,
and it really startled me.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.370
Booped? What does that mean?

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.620
Um, well, this.

00:18:58.620 --> 00:18:59.790
Boop.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.370
Miu!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.410
You're the best!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.370
Boop me, too!

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.450
What?

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.580
Are we really going to do that?

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:20.200
Before, we didn't get
many cheers from the audience.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.000
A great man said,
"Teamwork makes the dream work."

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.410
Sounds like fun!

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:25.950
I agree!

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:34.160
Okay, 22/7. Please go on standby.

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:36.370
Okay!

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:37.790
Okay, here we go!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:38.780
Wheat flour!

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:39.500
Pork!

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.950
C-Cabbage!

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:41.910
Chinese yam!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.160
Tenkasu!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.160
P-P-Pickled ginger!

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.200
Dried shrimp.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.330
Eggs.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.580
Just flip it over!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:53.410
22/7!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.330
"SHIN-OSAKA STATION"

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:04.120
Hey, why are you crying?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.540
Because you're leaving!

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:08.040
We're gonna miss you so much!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.750
Come home soon!

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.620
Yes! I'm gonna get Oguri's autograph.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.540
Man, you're the only one
happy about me leaving, ain't you?

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:20.040
Be sure to laugh a lot.
We may be poor, but laughter is free!

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.290
Okay!

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.830
Mom.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.200
Be well, Miyako.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:36.700
What's with that line?
Why are you being so nice?

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:39.080
It's not funny!

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:52.120
I'll find him for sure.

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:56.750
I'll find Dad,
and that'll make everyone happy again.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.580
That's not him.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.830
Miyako...

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:15.910
Let's go.

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.660
Okay, Mew-Mew!

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:22.450
Miyako, hurry up!

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:26.660
I ain't letting y'all take center on the bus!

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:28.000
Wha--

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:29.330
You have no ambition, do you?

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:30.580
Shut it!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.830
Wait, but where's
the center position for the bus?

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:35.160
I get motion sick,
so I'll take a window seat.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.790
It doesn't matter. Just sit, please!

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:40.950
Thanks to Miyako,
today's concert went really well.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.250
And Sakura seems better, too.
It's so strange.

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:49.410
Even though we're still not entirely sure why
we were gathered together in the first place...

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.410
Hang on, I'm busy right now.
I can't talk.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:56.500
Okay, okay. Got it.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:06.950
I can't help but think
that 22/7 needed all of us for something

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:09.620
and that's why we were gathered.

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:16.790
The eight of you were chosen.

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:20.000
We were chosen?

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:11.950
"Episode 6:
Between the Even and Odd Numbers"

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:11.950
"Between the Even and Odd Numbers."
